    "feedback": "Keep the 7-sensor layout (x = -0.03 to +0.03 m at 0.01 m spacing, 12 mm footprints, y = 0.05 m), the scaled weights [-2, -1.33, -0.67, 0, 0.67, 1.33, 2], and the kp 5 / kd 0.3 / ki 0.02 controller. These address the line-loss and steering-authority concerns from iteration 0, where every trial ended off_track with 1 to 2 line-loss events and max_error near the 0.06 m limit. Revise base_speed. A speed of 1.2 cannot cover the course in 300 steps: at 1.6 the robot only reached progress 0.10 to 0.15 before leaving the track, so the speed needed for completion has to come from fixing the drift, not from slowing down. Set base_speed to about 1.5 so the average speed stays near the roughly 1.5 m/s that finishing requires. Keep line_loss at last_direction. This revision is a judgement call that should be checked on the next race, not a verified fix. Once the revised design races, use progress and completion_time to decide whether 1.5 is still too slow or whether the drift returns at that speed, and use line_loss_events to confirm whether the wider sensors actually reduce line loss.",
